.TH STRAYNEKO 6

.SH NAME
strayneko \- desktop pet that wanders around your screen

.SH SYNOPSIS
.B strayneko
[\fB--help\fP]
[\fB--monitor\fP \fIn\fP]
[\fB--time\fP \fImicroseconds\fP]
[\fB--speed\fP \fIpixels\fP]
[\fB--min-wait\fP \fIseconds\fP]
[\fB--max-wait\fP \fIseconds\fP]
[\fB--bed\fP]
[\fB--fg\fP \fIcolor\fP]
[\fB--bg\fP \fIcolor\fP]
[\fB--noshape\fP]

.SH DESCRIPTION
.B strayneko
creates a small desktop pet that autonomously wanders around your desktop.
The cat alternates between idling, walking, sleeping, and occasional zoomies.
Unlike the original
.BR oneko ,
it does not chase the mouse cursor.

.SH OPTIONS

.TP
.B --help
Display the help message and exit.

.TP
.B --bed
Show a draggable bed that the cat may occasionally visit.

.TP
.BI --monitor " number"
Restrict the cat and bed to the specified XRandR monitor.

.TP
.BI --time " microseconds"
Set the animation interval.
The default is 125000 microseconds.

.TP
.BI --speed " pixels"
Set the maximum distance moved in one animation tick.
The default is 13 pixels.

.TP
.BI --min-wait " seconds"
Set the minimum idle time between walks.

.TP
.BI --max-wait " seconds"
Set the maximum idle time between walks.

.TP
.B --noshape
Disable the X11 SHAPE extension.

.TP
.BI --fg " color"
Set the cat outline color.

.TP
.BI --bg " color"
Set the cat body color.

.SH DEVELOPER OPTIONS
The following options are only available when strayneko is built with
.BR -DENABLE_DEBUG=ON .

.TP
.B --debug
Enables verbose debug logging.

.TP
.BI --force-target " x,y"
Forces the cat to move toward the specified coordinates.
Intended for debugging and testing only.

.SH X RESOURCES

The application name is
.B strayneko
and the class name is
.B Strayneko.

.TP
.B time
Animation interval in microseconds.

.TP
.B speed
Movement speed in pixels.

.TP
.B noshape
Disable the SHAPE extension.

.TP
.B foreground
Outline color.

.TP
.B background
Body color.

.SH AUTHOR

Original
.B xneko
was written by Masayuki Koba and later modified into
.B oneko
by Tatsuya Kato, John Lerchey, Eric Anderson, Toshihiro Kanda and Kiichiroh Mukose.

.PP
.B strayneko
is a modern fork created and maintained by
.B excommeownicado,
adding autonomous wandering, multi-monitor support, beds, configurable idle timing and other features while preserving the original authors' work.

